{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1537940-need-ideas-for-what-to-ask-from-spirits","id":1537940,"title":"Need Ideas for what to ask from Spirits","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-07-01T04:16:25-07:00","id":1537940,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon1.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Need Ideas for what to ask from Spirits","content":"Alright, so.<br /> <br /> <b>The scoop:</b><br /> <br /> I am playing a Rafastio Revenant in a game mostly populated by Kindred. Her reaction to being basically forced in participating in the current war efforts regarding the Sabbat is naturally to panic a fair bit.<br /> <br /> However, she has found her footing and now is making plays. One of these moves is a fairly major ritual involving spirit manipulation to call upon Weaver Spirits to help her establish her power base.<br /> <br /> Now, while I won't go into details, it is basically a multi levelled three-fold ritual in which she is offering the Spirits three trades of three different labor of three different kinds. (Hardware in the form of a robot she built, software in the form of a program she wrote and Organization in the form of the increased funding of the university's computer science department).<br /> <br /> That being said, while I have rough ideas and inclinations, I got kinda lost in making the ritual. As such, I would like to gather some inspiration on what would be reasonable to ask for. Time frame is 2002. To note, this is absolutely a &quot;the stars align, everything fits perfectly&quot; scenario. The total amount of effort to produce and create everything involved was about 2 months of daily work *on something*.<br /> <br /> Naturally, in the end it is up to the ST, but I like to come in with some ground ideas that we can work together on, take the initiative and all that.<br /> <br /> Thx for replies!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28457-xasure","name":"Xasure","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-01T06:52:41-07:00","id":1537945,"title":"","content":"Depends on what the actual goal for the attack is of course, but if I had to pick three boons to get for any hack:<br /> <br /> - Location: You want to know which system(s) to target, and in what way. Hollywood-hacks always underestimate how much legwork can be involved in this and how time consuming it can be. If you have a Spirit doing the legwork of locating and probing the system for you, you save a lot of time and are able to execute the hack quickly.<br /> <br /> - Access: Manipulation, control, and all the other fun stuff hinges on being able to properly access the system. You can get one of the Weaver Spirits to act as a smart backdoor agent. Magic is great for circumventing mundane security limitations, and since you're going after another supernatural target, you also want a Spirit with some oomph. At least expect it might run into thaumaturgical wards and look for a Spirit that can circumvent them. I recommend taking a look at <i>WtA:Book of the Weaver</i> which lists several fitting Weaver Spirits.<br /> <br /> - Reach: Ideally you want your manipulation to distribute itself to connected systems. With Spirits/magic you enjoy the option of otherwise impossible distribution vectors. Consider things like spreading misinformation through a Meme Spirit (yes, that's a thing) or remotely bugging Sabbat Nokias.<br /> <br /> Edit: After thinking about it, if your goal is to establish a power base - consider using the Ritual to gain a Weaver Spirit as a Familiar instead of three one-time favors. That way you have an ally who can continuously support you, and my experience with having a Weaver Spirit Familiar is that they are extremely useful for scouting, information gathering, and light infiltration of electronic devices. You even have a robot they can possess or nest in so it could assist you physically to a degree. Not sure if there are good sources for Vampire on Familiars, but Mage has a few: <i>Gods &amp; Monsters</i> is the M20 version, but I personally prefer the rules in <i>Forged by Dragons Fire</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":27477,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","user":"voidshaper","date":". 07-02-2024, 06:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-13T13:46:31-07:00","id":1538537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1537940-need-ideas-for-what-to-ask-from-spirits?p=1537945#post1537945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Depends on what the actual goal for the attack is of course, but if I had to pick three boons to get for any hack:<br /> <br /> - Location: You want to know which system(s) to target, and in what way. Hollywood-hacks always underestimate how much legwork can be involved in this and how time consuming it can be. If you have a Spirit doing the legwork of locating and probing the system for you, you save a lot of time and are able to execute the hack quickly.<br /> <br /> - Access: Manipulation, control, and all the other fun stuff hinges on being able to properly access the system. You can get one of the Weaver Spirits to act as a smart backdoor agent. Magic is great for circumventing mundane security limitations, and since you're going after another supernatural target, you also want a Spirit with some oomph. At least expect it might run into thaumaturgical wards and look for a Spirit that can circumvent them. I recommend taking a look at <i>WtA:Book of the Weaver</i> which lists several fitting Weaver Spirits.<br /> <br /> - Reach: Ideally you want your manipulation to distribute itself to connected systems. With Spirits/magic you enjoy the option of otherwise impossible distribution vectors. Consider things like spreading misinformation through a Meme Spirit (yes, that's a thing) or remotely bugging Sabbat Nokias.<br /> <br /> Edit: After thinking about it, if your goal is to establish a power base - consider using the Ritual to gain a Weaver Spirit as a Familiar instead of three one-time favors. That way you have an ally who can continuously support you, and my experience with having a Weaver Spirit Familiar is that they are extremely useful for scouting, information gathering, and light infiltration of electronic devices. You even have a robot they can possess or nest in so it could assist you physically to a degree. Not sure if there are good sources for Vampire on Familiars, but Mage has a few: <i>Gods &amp; Monsters</i> is the M20 version, but I personally prefer the rules in <i>Forged by Dragons Fire</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Terribly sorry for the late response, life suplexed me a bit.<br /> <br /> Yes, the intent is to more establish means of building up. In part because in comparison to the Kindred in the game, she is by her own nature limited in terms of power.<br /> <br /> A familiar was something I was considering but due to the lacking rules for V20 in that regard, not sure if I could convince the STs on that front. (Matter of fact, one of the offerings she has is a small robot spider that she created and which she hoped could serve as a medium of communication)<br /> <br /> Another idea was for her to ask for the creation of something of a local version of <i>FangChat</i><b>. </b> Because the local Tower has... well, they are all relatively young and tend to use mobiles and such extensively. Having a means of communication that isn\u00b4t subject to the usual problems is a valuable commodity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28457-xasure","name":"Xasure","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-17T14:44:35-07:00","id":1538792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xasure</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1537940-need-ideas-for-what-to-ask-from-spirits?p=1538537#post1538537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A familiar was something I was considering but due to the lacking rules for V20 in that regard, not sure if I could convince the STs on that front. (Matter of fact, one of the offerings she has is a small robot spider that she created and which she hoped could serve as a medium of communication)</div> </div> </div> </div>There is really little in V20 material on familiars. There are <i>Blood Familiars</i> in Guide to the Tal'Mahe'Ra which are a completely different thing and fall under Things An ST Will Give You a Funny Look If You Ask For Them, but at least there is an historic connection between the Rafastio and the True Black Hand. There is a Thaumaturgy Ritual in VDA20 for binding an animal familiar. I think it wouldn't hurt to ask the ST, if you can not use the rules from Mage you should at least be able to treat it as a supernatural Retainer (Background), essentially on par with a Ghoul.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xasure</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1537940-need-ideas-for-what-to-ask-from-spirits?p=1538537#post1538537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another idea was for her to ask for the creation of something of a local version of <i>FangChat</i><b>. </b> Because the local Tower has... well, they are all relatively young and tend to use mobiles and such extensively. Having a means of communication that isn\u00b4t subject to the usual problems is a valuable commodity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Any kind of enhanced infrastructure is also a good idea. Basically, consider the three points I mentioned earlier and implement measures to prevent them being used against you. If you are concerned with comsec, asking a Weaver Spirit to act as messenger to magically encrypt and transport the information between devices is a pretty secure way to prevent interception - unless there happen to be some Glasswalker Garou around, in which case you have other problems. They are at least very unlikely to leak any info to other vampires.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}